            "property_name": "Study period",
            "property_type": "epoch",
            "property_comment": "Top header band naming study phases: Screening (col 2), Treatment Period (merged across cols 3-15, Day -1 to ED), Follow-Up phone call (col 16). Phase names -> epoch. Label cell empty; name synthesized."
          },
          {
            "hierarchical_level": 2,
            "property_name": "Study day",
            "property_type": "study_day",
            "property_comment": "Study-day row: '-28 to -2 days prior to Day 1' (Screening), Day -1, Days 1-11, ED (early discontinuation), and for the Follow-Up column the window 'within 7 to 10 days after last dose' (vertically merged across rows 2-3 in the source). Numeric day labels -> study_day. The printed label cell reads 'Procedure', which heads the activity column, so the property name is synthesized."
          },
          {
            "hierarchical_level": null,
            "property_name": "Days",
            "property_type": "other",
            "property_comment": "Presentational band carrying the single spanning label 'Days' over cols 3-15, qualifying the numbers in row 3 as study days. It does not by itself distinguish any two columns, so hierarchical_level is null. Label cell empty; name taken from the spanning value."
          }
        ]
